CORE broken-smt-backend
blocking_flag_in_loop2.sv
--bound 0
^\[main\.p0\] .*: PROVED up to bound 0$
^\[main\.p1\] .*: PROVED up to bound 0$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
--
The definitions of out, valid and found share subexpressions, which the
lowering of each definition used to copy, and the propositional encoding
then compared the copies structurally, which takes time exponential in
the number of iterations. The SMT backends do not finish in reasonable
time on it.
